AI Plugins for Design Concepts & Massing in Revit — Beginner Guide (Windows)
This tutorial focuses specifically on Revit and the two real categories of AI tools people mean when they say "AI plugins for Revit":
Path A — Autodesk AI (Autodesk Forma): Autodesk's own AI-driven massing/site generator, connected to Revit via an official extension. Best starting point — no coding, fully supported.
Path B — Chatbot-style AI (Dynamo + ChatGPT/LLM node): A conversational AI plugin inside Revit's visual scripting tool (Dynamo) that lets you type natural-language prompts to help generate or adjust parametric massing logic.
Path C — Third-party generative feasibility (TestFit): An external AI tool purpose-built for fast massing/unit-mix studies, which exports directly into Dynamo/Revit.
You'll set up and use all three at a beginner level, so you understand the real landscape rather than just one tool.
---
Prerequisites
Windows 10/11, 64-bit
Revit 2024–2026 installed
An Autodesk Account (for Forma — free trial tier available)
Revit's built-in Dynamo (ships free with Revit — no separate install)
An OpenAI API key if you want to try Path B's ChatGPT node (free to create, pay-per-use)
A TestFit account (free trial) if trying Path C
Stable internet connection (all three are cloud-connected)
---
PATH A — Autodesk AI (Forma) → Revit
Step 1: Create a Forma proposal
Go to `forma.autodesk.com`, sign in with your Autodesk ID.
Click New Proposal, search your site address — Forma auto-pulls terrain and context.
Use the Site Boundary tool (dashed-polygon icon) to trace your property line; double-click to close it, `Esc` to exit.
Step 2: Verify your Access and Location to create Building Design Data for AI purposes
Goto AutoDesk Forma Design URL: https://forma.aus.autodesk.com/app-home?utm_source=aum
Click on Building Design Button and try to enter program inputs (target GFA, floor count, building type, setbacks).
Next steps will be shared in the classroom session...
Step 3: Bring it into Revit - "Please Hold-Off on below steps"
In Revit: `Add-Ins` tab → check for Forma panel. If missing, install "Forma extension for Revit" from the Autodesk App Store, restart Revit.
Click `Forma` → `Get Massing`, sign in, pick your saved proposal, click Import.
It arrives as an in-place mass, geo-positioned automatically.
Convert it: select the mass → `Massing & Site` tab → `Model by Face` → `Wall` / `Floor` / `Roof`.
Commands & shortcuts - These will be explained in the Classroom sessions
Action	Shortcut/Path
Show/hide mass	`GM`
Wall by Face	`WF`
Floor/Roof by Face	`Massing & Site` → `Model by Face`
Zoom extents	`ZE`
3D view	`3D`
