PATH B — Chatbot-style AI Plugin (Dynamo + ChatGPT node)
This is the literal "ChatBot in Revit" experience: a Dynamo custom node exists that calls the ChatGPT API for chat completion directly inside your Dynamo graph, which drives Revit geometry.
Step 1: Open Dynamo from Revit
In Revit, go to `Manage` tab → `Visual Programming` panel → click Dynamo.
Dynamo opens in a new window. Click New to start a blank graph.
Step 2: Install the ChatGPT node package
In Dynamo, go to `Packages` menu → `Search for a Package`.
Search for a ChatGPT/OpenAI completion node package (community packages exist under names like "ChatGPT" or "OpenAI Dynamo").
Click Install, accept the terms, restart Dynamo when prompted.
Step 3: Wire up your first AI-assisted prompt
Drag the ChatGPT node onto the canvas.
Add a Code Block or String node, type your prompt in quotes, e.g. `"Suggest 3 massing strategies for a 4-story mixed-use building on a narrow urban infill site"`.
Connect the String node's output to the ChatGPT node's prompt input.
Add your API key into the node's key input field (or a String node feeding it) — never hardcode it into a graph you'll share publicly.
Run the graph (`F5` or the Run button, bottom-left of Dynamo).
The node returns text output — use it as design guidance, or parse specific numbers (like unit counts or floor heights) into downstream nodes that actually generate massing geometry (e.g., `Solid.ByLoft`, `Cuboid.ByLengths`) parametrically.
Commands & shortcuts (Dynamo)
Action	Shortcut
Run graph	`F5`
Pan canvas	Hold middle mouse button, drag
Zoom	Mouse scroll wheel
Search node library	`Ctrl+Space`
Delete selected node	`Delete`
Undo	`Ctrl+Z`
