If Something Goes Wrong
Problem	Fix
Forma panel missing from Revit's Add-Ins tab	Reinstall the Forma extension from Autodesk App Store; confirm same Autodesk ID signed in everywhere; restart Revit.
ChatGPT node in Dynamo returns an error/blank	Check your API key is valid and has available quota/credits; confirm internet connection; check the prompt input is a valid String node, not disconnected.
Dynamo graph won't run (`F5` does nothing)	Look for red-outlined nodes — these have missing/invalid inputs; hover to see the error tooltip.
Forma "Get Massing" import fails/times out	Ensure your Forma proposal is fully saved (not mid-edit) in-browser before importing; check connection.
Imported mass appears in wrong location	`Manage` → `Location` → `Site Location`; confirm it matches your Forma/TestFit project address; re-import.
TestFit-to-Dynamo import produces nothing	Confirm you exported to the correct format/package version expected by your Dynamo graph; re-check TestFit's export settings.
Revit slows down after several AI imports	`Manage` → `Purge Unused`; delete earlier rejected mass imports you no longer need.
"Model by Face" does nothing when clicked	You selected an edge/vertex, not a face — click a flat mass surface directly, then retry.
---
Quick Recap
`Forma (Autodesk AI): site → AI massing options → Sun/Wind/Noise analysis → Get Massing into Revit`
`Dynamo (ChatGPT node): open Dynamo → install ChatGPT package → prompt → parse into geometry nodes`
`TestFit (AI feasibility): typology + program → AI-optimized massing → export via Dynamo/Revit → Model by Face`
All three converge on the same final Revit step: convert imported/generated massing into real walls, floors, and roofs via `Model by Face`, then continue detailed BIM work as normal.
